# <type>(<scope>): <summary>
#
# Summary rules:
# - Use English.
# - Use imperative style where possible.
# - Keep the header under 90 characters.
# - Do not mention AI-generated code.
# - Avoid vague summaries such as "update files", "changes", "fix stuff", or "misc".
#
# Allowed types:
# - feat: user-visible capability
# - fix: bug fix
# - refactor: behavior-preserving code restructuring
# - test: tests or test fixtures
# - docs: documentation only
# - style: formatting or visual style with no behavior change
# - chore: maintenance
# - build: build system or dependency plumbing
# - ci: CI configuration
# - perf: performance improvement
# - revert: revert a previous commit
#
# Recommended scopes:
# jobs, applications, profile, notifications, storage, sync, plugins, mcp,
# ai, ui, auth, docs, repo, tauri, angular
#
# Examples:
# feat(jobs): add saved jobs empty state
# fix(storage): preserve application notes during migration
# docs(ai): add commit workflow
# chore(repo): update generated ignore patterns
#
# Body guidance:
# - Explain what changed and why when the header is not enough.
# - Mention behavior or risk when touching privacy, storage, sync, auth,
#   notifications, plugins, MCP, external sources, or user data.
# - Recommend splitting the commit if unrelated changes are staged.
#
# Footer examples:
# BREAKING CHANGE: describe the migration or incompatible behavior.
# Closes #123
